  {
   "uuid": "8db3190c-15c5-4b99-81b3-dc5d73114281",
   "text": "",
   "content": [
    {
     "start_timestamp": "2026-10-01T04:45:02.000000Z",
     "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-01T04:45:22.952000Z",
     "type": "text",
     "text": "For a half with your volume, a two-week taper that cuts volume but keeps some intensity:\n\n**Week of Oct 5 (10 days out)**\n- Total volume ~70% of normal (≈ 7 h).\n- Keep one quality session: e.g., Tue 3 × 2 km at half-marathon pace (~4:02/km) with 2 min jog.\n- Long run 75 min easy, a few strides.\n\n**Race week (Oct 12–15)**\n- Volume ~40–50% of normal.\n- Mon: 40 min easy.\n- Tue: 30 min easy + 4 × 1 km at race pace, full recovery.\n- Wed: 20–30 min easy + 4 strides, or rest if you feel flat.\n- Thu: **race**.\n\nPrinciples: cut volume, not intensity entirely; keep frequency similar so you don't feel stale; drop cycling in race week unless it's very easy spinning.\n\nSub-1:25 = 6:29/mile, 4:02/km. If your threshold workouts have been at ~6:15–6:20/mile, that goal is realistic.",
     "citations": []
    }
   ],
