     "type": "text",
     "text": "Those splits suggest you're in shape for something around 1:22–1:24, depending on the course and the day. A sensible plan: go out at 6:25–6:28 for the first 5 km, check how it feels, and only push from mile 8 if you're still controlled. Starting at 1:22 pace and fading costs more than a negative split gains.",
